<section class="shell content-section split-content"><div class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">THE TERRACE WAY</span><h2>Belonging is on the menu.</h2><p>Founded in 1904, Terrace F. Club is a non-selective eating club at Princeton University. Members share meals, social events, live music, and an accepting community in the clubhouse at 62 Washington Road.</p><p>Members call each other Terrans, the clubhouse “the Mother,” and the feeling that ties it together <strong>FOOD = LOVE</strong>. The club’s meals include vegetarian and vegan options, and its stage has a long history of memorable shows.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="/contact/">Find us <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><img src="/images/clubhouse-snow.jpg" alt="The Terrace Club clubhouse on a snowy evening" width="900" height="900" /></section>
